# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# roughness_demo.mac — make the pTP surface roughness (sigmaAlpha) visible.
#
# sigmaAlpha is NOT a geometric feature: Geant4's UNIFIED model keeps the pTP
# faces flat and tilts the micro-facet normal by a random angle (RMS sigmaAlpha)
# at every surface crossing. It can therefore only be seen through the photon
# directions. This demo sends a 400 nm beam — which the pTP film does NOT absorb,
# so the beam goes through the sample — with an exaggerated sigmaAlpha = 0.8 rad
# (~46°): instead of staying collimated to the PMT, the transmitted beam fans out
# behind the sample. Compare with roughness_off.mac (sigmaAlpha = 0, 128 nm).
#
# Qt session:  Run menu → "Roughness demo"  (or /control/execute roughness_demo.mac)
# Measured (2000 photons, 400 nm): photons leaving layer 1 within 2.6° of the
# axis — 99.7 % at sigmaAlpha 0, 1.9 % at 0.3 rad, 0.4 % at 0.8 rad.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/detector/pTPsigmaAlpha 0.8
/run/reinitializeGeometry
/run/initialize
/vis/viewer/rebuild
/gps/particle opticalphoton
/gps/energy 3.0996 eV
/gps/pos/type Plane
/gps/pos/shape Circle
/gps/pos/centre 0. 0. -2. cm
/gps/pos/radius 7 mm
/gps/direction 0 0 1
/run/beamOn 40
